{
  "id": "fyrtf1a",
  "title": "Chapter 6: COAL AND PETROLEUM",
  "order": 26,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "fccs76n",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Natural Resources"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Fossil fuels like coal, petroleum, and natural gas are exhaustible natural resources formed from dead organisms under high pressure and temperature over millions of years.",
        "Coke is a tough, porous, black substance and is an almost pure form of carbon used in steel manufacturing.",
        "Petroleum refining separates crude oil into fractions like LPG, petrol, kerosene, diesel, lubricating oil, and paraffin wax based on boiling points.",
        "Compressed Natural Gas (CNG) is a clean fuel stored under high pressure and causes significantly less air pollution than liquid fossil fuels.",
        "Combustion requires three necessary conditions: a combustible substance, air/oxygen, and attainment of the ignition temperature."
      ],
      "id": "t22ommy"
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "Calorific Value Unit",
          "value": "kJ/kg",
          "icon": "award"
        },
        {
          "label": "Formation Period",
          "value": "Millions of Years",
          "icon": "calendar"
        },
        {
          "label": "Road Surfacing Material",
          "value": "Bitumen",
          "icon": "info"
        },
        {
          "label": "PCRA Standard",
          "value": "Moderate Speed Driving",
          "icon": "check"
        }
      ],
      "id": "63cezev"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2v5hjfm",
      "content": "Natural resources are substances obtained from nature and used by humans."
    },
    {
      "id": "f1smyz4",
      "type": "image",
      "imageId": "0x7mze2",
      "src": "/books/Precis/RRB GS/images/image_0x7mze2.png"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8sq5cgf",
      "content": "They are classified into Inexhaustible and Exhaustible resources."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "emisvus",
      "content": "Coal, petroleum and natural gas are exhaustible fossil fuels."
    },
    {
      "id": "1p85yu6",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Fossil Fuels"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "v42v73b",
      "content": "Fossil fuels are formed from dead plants and animals buried under earth millions of years ago."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "53m0dqf",
      "content": "They were formed under high temperature and pressure in absence of air."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1k30ro2",
      "content": "Examples: Coal, Petroleum, Natural Gas."
    },
    {
      "id": "gfkn6vt",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. Coal"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hb5fvqf",
      "content": "Coal is a black solid fossil fuel formed from ancient vegetation."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "intyqu1",
      "content": "Formation of coal from dead plants is called Carbonisation."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fj5n1rn",
      "content": "Coal mainly contains carbon along with hydrogen, oxygen, nitrogen and sulphur."
    },
    {
      "id": "5za1mo2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Products of Coal"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kmhdh44",
      "content": "When coal is heated in absence of air (destructive distillation), the following are obtained:"
    },
    {
      "id": "3zbvu67",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Coke",
        "Coal Tar",
        "Coal Gas"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lxjfr19",
      "type": "image",
      "imageId": "bc5p5ky",
      "src": "/books/Precis/RRB GS/images/image_bc5p5ky.png"
    },
    {
      "id": "6ewig16",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Coke"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "icix1rt",
      "content": "Coke is almost pure carbon."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qtpof9f",
      "content": "It is porous, tough and black."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "x2r3bpi",
      "content": "Used in manufacture of steel and extraction of metals."
    },
    {
      "id": "dl1phv6",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Coal Tar"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "p6efctb",
      "content": "Coal tar is a thick black liquid with unpleasant smell."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "w32tgcp",
      "content": "It contains about 200 substances."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jb9o2fm",
      "content": "Used in manufacture of dyes, drugs, explosives, perfumes, plastics, naphthalene and roads."
    },
    {
      "id": "lxr8sqz",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Coal Gas"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2jcfj00",
      "content": "Coal gas is used as fuel in industries near coal processing plants."
    },
    {
      "id": "65po7p6",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. Petroleum"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pc2npqs",
      "content": "Petroleum is a dark oily liquid found deep inside earth."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sw90875",
      "content": "It is also called crude oil."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ygz3vmg",
      "content": "It is a mixture of various hydrocarbons."
    },
    {
      "id": "x57x4nc",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Refining of Petroleum"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fsbz18n",
      "content": "Refining is the process of separating different useful components from crude oil."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mjxd9h1",
      "content": "It is done by fractional distillation in a refinery column."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "34im82o",
      "content": "Different fractions are obtained at different boiling points."
    },
    {
      "id": "dor7ud7",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5. Petroleum Fractions"
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Fossil fuels are exhaustible natural resources formed from the dead remains of living organisms over millions of years.",
      "id": "oojlvad"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6u3kziz",
      "content": "The lighter fractions are obtained at top of column and heavier at bottom."
    },
    {
      "id": "f0kvmkv",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. Natural Gas"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "uv2edmm",
      "content": "Natural gas is mainly methane (CH4)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lia8fbk",
      "content": "It is a clean fuel and produces less pollution."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "89v6hsh",
      "content": "It is stored as CNG (Compressed Natural Gas)."
    },
    {
      "id": "h7fcsw1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Advantages of CNG"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "8u05c1c",
      "content": "- High calorific value"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "8h62kg7",
      "content": "- Burns without smoke"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "bcpx3nx",
      "content": "- Less pollution"
    },
    {
      "id": "6uwrsd4",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. Petrochemicals"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kp2dh2i",
      "content": "Petrochemicals are chemicals obtained from petroleum and natural gas."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5cgi85s",
      "content": "Used in manufacture of plastics, synthetic fibres, detergents, rubber, fertilizers etc."
    },
    {
      "id": "56tc6pv",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Non-renewable Nature & Conservation"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "p5x55b4",
      "content": "Coal and petroleum are non-renewable resources."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4wjpt0l",
      "content": "They take millions of years to form."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5ccn3ux",
      "content": "Conservation is necessary for future generations."
    },
    {
      "id": "qawm9ld",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Petroleum Conservation Tips"
    },
    {
